Subject: [Krypton] Default-off optional-feature registry and native settings

Helium keeps the listed optional features disabled. Register default-false
Local State choices without changing any feature decision, capture immutable
startup state after Local State loads, and expose only usable feature records
through the optional native settings contract. With every switch off this
plumbing makes no network requests and leaves Helium's feature gates intact.

